user:piuser
broker ip: 192.168.2.100

Credentials:
- Firmware links the shared precompiled
  `../../libraries/Credentials/src/cortex-m0plus/libCredentials.a` library.
- An existing private library is used unchanged. For a fresh checkout, run
  `../scripts/setup-credentials.sh` from this directory, fill the generated
  `../../libraries/Credentials/config/*.local.*` files, then build it with
  `../../libraries/Credentials/scripts/build.sh rp2040`.
- `../libraries/Credentials` under `lights-timer/` is a complete, secret-free
  bootstrap template and is not part of the active TimerNTP build.

Build model:
- `TimerNTP.ino` was removed from the source tree.
- Application entry now lives in `TimerNTP.cpp` and implements the JaszczurHAL
  `app_start()` / `app_task0()` contract.
- `hal_project_config.h` enables `HAL_PROVIDE_APP_ENTRY`, so JaszczurHAL owns
  Arduino `setup()` / `loop()`.
- CMake generates a temporary Arduino sketch under `.build/cmake/sketch/TimerNTP`
  only for `arduino-cli`. Do not edit or commit files from `.build`.

Build commands:
- Config dump: `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode config-dump --project .`
- Build firmware: `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode build --project .`
- Build debug firmware: `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode build-debug --project .`
- Serial upload: `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode upload --project .`
- BOOTSEL UF2 upload: `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode upload-uf2 --project .`
- OTA discovery: `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode ota-discover --project .`
- OTA upload: set `TIMER_NTP_OTA_PASSWORD`, then run
  `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode upload-ota --project .`
- Refresh VS Code IntelliSense: `../../libraries/JaszczurHAL/vscode/entry/jh-vscode refresh-intellisense --project .`

Build artifacts:
- `.build/firmware.elf`
- `.build/firmware.bin`
- `.build/firmware.uf2`
- `.build/firmware.ota`
- `.build/firmware.map`

OTA trial policy:
- The OTA service starts after WiFi is available, preserving a network recovery
  path while the rest of product startup is still running.
- Discovery uses the LAN-directed `192.168.2.255` broadcast because the build
  host also has a WireGuard interface and limited broadcast was unreliable.
- Upload targets the board's reserved `192.168.2.171` address directly; this
  avoids ambiguity when other OTA-capable devices are online.
- Device UDP and host TCP callback ports are both pinned to `8266`; the LAN and
  host firewall must permit the device to initiate that TCP connection.
- A trial image is confirmed only after TimerNTP reaches `STATE_CONNECTED`,
  which means WiFi, NTP, WireGuard and MQTT startup checks have completed.
- If those checks never complete, the image remains unconfirmed and the native
  OTA boot applier can roll it back after the configured retry limit.

